                            <comment id="497152" author="adilger" created="Wed, 1 Jul 2026 18:48:39 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=arshad512" class="user-hover" rel="arshad512"&gt;arshad512&lt;/a&gt;, would you be able to work on implementing the &lt;tt&gt;FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE&lt;/tt&gt; functionality for ZFS, preferably as a precursor to the space reservation, because it fits with existing ZFS functionality and it is needed for proper "&lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror resync&lt;/tt&gt;" operation for sparse mirror and/or EC files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think the existing patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/36506" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/36506&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14157" title="Implement fallocate() support for zfs Lustre" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14157"&gt;LU-14157&lt;/a&gt; zfs-osd: Add fallocate functionality for ZFS") implements most of the needed infrastructure, but it should be modified to only allow the &lt;tt&gt;PUNCH_HOLE&lt;/tt&gt; operation to start. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497171" author="arshad512" created="Thu, 2 Jul 2026 05:42:35 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Thanks for bringing this up. ACK. Will focus on PUNCH_HOLE support.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PS: I do not recollect immediately. However, I will check and add (in Gerrit) why regular mode 0 fallocate was stalled."&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
